  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Huntington Ingalls obligated $3B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date, across 67 awards with an average award size of $44.1M. Obligations are down 29.5% year over year. Ship Building and Repairing is the dominant market, accounting for $2.8B of obligations so far. Huntington Ingalls has a multi-year profile of stable-to-rising obligations before the current-year drop: obligations were $3.6B in FY21, $3B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.6B in FY24, and $4.2B in FY25. Engineering Services and Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance are present but much smaller markets, with $58.4M and $41.1M respectively. Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing appears at $7.5M. Hardware Manufacturing shows $0 in obligations for the current period. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity rather than a full fiscal year tally.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Huntington Ingalls' federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls obligated $3B in FY2026 to date, down 29.5% year over year. Huntington Ingalls peaked at $4.2B in FY25 after a series of $3B to $3.6B years from FY21 through FY24. The FY2026 to date total reflects partial-year activity and a concentration in Ship Building and Repairing at $2.8B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Huntington Ingalls' largest markets and award characteristics?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing is the largest market with $2.8B in obligations. Huntington Ingalls also has $58.4M in Engineering Services and $41.1M in Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance, with smaller amounts in Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $7.5M and $0 in Hardware Manufacturing. The 67 awards so far average $44.1M each."
      }
    ]
  },
